  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466494",
      "title": "Adding Routes to Feature Modules",
      "lectureOrder": 650,
      "videoOrder": 598,
      "sourceHash": "514ad1aa05bbaf8abb40add023bb94c49552e642d98ded64ef54331f87a47899",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "Instructor: Now the work we did",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 6.69,
          "en": "on the recipes module was a good start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.69,
          "end": 8.82,
          "en": "but of course the only thing we're doing thus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.82,
          "end": 13.82,
          "en": "far is we're outsourcing our recipes component declaration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.89,
          "end": 17.22,
          "en": "in a separate module so that the app module is a bit leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.22,
          "end": 20.1,
          "en": "Now, that wouldn't be the worst reason to do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.1,
          "end": 23.25,
          "en": "It's absolutely fine to restructure your app to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.25,
          "end": 25.95,
          "en": "have leaner modules that are easier to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.95,
          "end": 27.3,
          "en": "and to manage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.3,
          "end": 30.81,
          "en": "Yet we can actually do more than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.81,
          "end": 34.53,
          "en": "We can also move the recipes related route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.53,
          "end": 38.43,
          "en": "configuration away from the app routing module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 41.16,
          "en": "So I'm talking about this branch here essentially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.16,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "Away from the app routing module and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 45.573,
          "en": "into our recipes module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.41,
          "end": 50.31,
          "en": "For that, here in the router module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.31,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "you could add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 52.583,
          "en": "forChild",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.63,
          "end": 55.56,
          "en": "now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.56,
          "end": 58.59,
          "en": "Now forRoot is only used once, essentially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.59,
          "end": 60.51,
          "en": "here in the app routing module where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.51,
          "end": 63.78,
          "en": "we use forRoot to configure our root routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.78,
          "end": 66.99,
          "en": "in a feature module, which you then plan",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.99,
          "end": 70.77,
          "en": "on importing into your app module you would use forChild",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.77,
          "end": 73.14,
          "en": "and this will automatically merge the child",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.14,
          "end": 76.77,
          "en": "routing configuration with the root routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.77,
          "end": 79.56,
          "en": "So therefore, here we can use forChild",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.56,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "and passing that same array of route configuration we pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 84.42,
          "en": "to for route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.42,
          "end": 88.32,
          "en": "Now to keep this file leaner, and this is totally optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.32,
          "end": 90.3,
          "en": "I'll again create a separate module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.3,
          "end": 94.14,
          "en": "the recipes-routing.module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.14,
          "end": 96,
          "en": "and therefore I'll export this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96,
          "end": 99.53999999999999,
          "en": "Recipes routing module, which will receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.53999999999999,
          "end": 102.3,
          "en": "the @NgModule decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.3,
          "end": 106.08,
          "en": "And I only do that to focus on the route setup in this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.08,
          "end": 110.16,
          "en": "and not clutter the other recipes module file with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.16,
          "end": 113.13,
          "en": "So here we have our routes, which are of type routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.13,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "which is imported from at @angular/router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 116.55,
          "en": "and which is an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.55,
          "end": 120.03,
          "en": "And in that array you add all recipes related routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.03,
          "end": 122.85,
          "en": "And in this case, if we have a look at the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.85,
          "end": 127.85,
          "en": "routing module, that means I take this single route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.1,
          "end": 130.68,
          "en": "this recipes route with all its nested routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 133.92,
          "en": "I take that, cut it from my app routing module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.92,
          "end": 137.4,
          "en": "and move it here into the recipes routing module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.4,
          "end": 141.693,
          "en": "So now here we have that route file, that route set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.819,
          "end": 146.4,
          "en": "That of course means that all these imports have to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.4,
          "end": 149.643,
          "en": "be added, and I will add all missing imports here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.14,
          "end": 154.56,
          "en": "So all the recipe components and also the AuthGuard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.56,
          "end": 156.9,
          "en": "that's all important, we used that here too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.9,
          "end": 158.91,
          "en": "So that this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.91,
          "end": 160.98,
          "en": "now has a correct route setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.98,
          "end": 164.67000000000002,
          "en": "And now in @NgModule, we add imports and import the router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.67000000000002,
          "end": 168.84,
          "en": "module from at @angular/router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.84,
          "end": 172.14,
          "en": "And as I just explained on that module, you now call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.14,
          "end": 174.39,
          "en": "forChild and passing your routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.39,
          "end": 179.39,
          "en": "And then just before, you export this router module here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.94,
          "end": 182.7,
          "en": "We exported in the recipes routing module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.7,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "so that in the recipes module we can actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "import our recipes routing module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 189.894,
          "en": "And again, of course for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.894,
          "end": 192.963,
          "en": "you need to add an import path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.92,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "So import recipes routing module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 199.95,
          "en": "from the recipes-routing.module file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.95,
          "end": 204.32999999999998,
          "en": "So now we're adding the routes here in the recipes area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.32999999999998,
          "end": 208.86,
          "en": "Now, with that adjustment in the app routing module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 210.81,
          "en": "we got one route less.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.81,
          "end": 213.48,
          "en": "We got all the other routes, but not this route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.48,
          "end": 217.89,
          "en": "But now in the app module, we do import the recipes module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.89,
          "end": 221.67000000000002,
          "en": "And since we register our recipes related routes there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.67000000000002,
          "end": 224.73,
          "en": "they should still be part of our general routing conflict.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 224.73,
          "end": 226.68,
          "en": "The conflict, the routing conflict,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 229.53,
          "en": "is now just split across two files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.53,
          "end": 231.48,
          "en": "That also means that here in the re --",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 233.25,
          "en": "in the app routing module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.25,
          "end": 237.93,
          "en": "we remove all these unused imports so that they don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.93,
          "end": 239.883,
          "en": "well pollute this file anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 242.433,
          "en": "Now let's try saving that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.93,
          "end": 244.95,
          "en": "And this looks good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.95,
          "end": 248.16,
          "en": "Here I'm in the recipes area and I can navigate around,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 248.16,
          "end": 249.51,
          "en": "I can go to new recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.51,
          "end": 251.85,
          "en": "So all these recipe related routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.85,
          "end": 255.09,
          "en": "they still work just as did it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 255.09,
          "end": 259.14,
          "en": "But now with our split up route conflict, and again here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.14,
          "end": 261.78,
          "en": "the idea can be that we make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.78,
          "end": 264.33,
          "en": "that we have a leaner app module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.33,
          "end": 266.55,
          "en": "and a leaner app routing module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.55,
          "end": 269.46,
          "en": "and we manage all recipes related things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 269.46,
          "end": 272.853,
          "en": "in our recipes module and nowhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
